Here's the result of `get_context`:

```json
{
  "Environment": "production",
  "Org": "personal",
  "Project": {
    "name": "wakil-acceptance",
    "org": "personal",
    "environments": {
      "production": {
        "databases": [
          { "driver": "mysql", "name": "core", "readOnly": true, "ref": "acc-prod-core" }
        ]
      },
      "staging": {
        "api": { "baseUrl": "https://httpbin.org" },
        "databases": [
          { "driver": "mysql",  "name": "core",   "readOnly": true, "ref": "acc-staging-core" },
          { "driver": "sqlite", "name": "events", "readOnly": true, "ref": "acc-staging-events" },
          { "driver": "mongo",  "name": "docs",   "readOnly": true, "ref": "acc-staging-docs" }
        ]
      }
    },
    "roots": [
      { "path": "/Users/operator/wakil.acceptance",     "role": "api" },
      { "path": "/Users/operator/wakil.acceptance/src", "role": "web" }
    ],
    "scopes": {
      "pm": { "projectKey": "INI", "provider": "jira" }
    }
  },
  "ProjectPath": "/Users/operator/wakil.acceptance/.wakil/project.json",
  "Provider": {
    "match": true,
    "running": "main",
    "note": "this project names no provider and the org has no default"
  }
}
```

A few things worth noting:

- **Active environment is `production`** — it exposes only the read-only `acc-prod-core` MySQL database, and no API base URL. The richer `staging` environment (3 databases + an httpbin API endpoint) is not active.
- **Project roots point at `/Users/operator/wakil.acceptance`**, which is a different tree from this worktree (`/Users/operator/conductor/workspaces/wakil/sacramento`).
- **Provider report says `match: true`** with `running: "main"` — trivially satisfied, since neither the project nor the org names a preferred provider.

